feedback\": \"This is a reasonable low-confidence reservoir variant because mol_010 is reported in the Shen annulation chemistry. But rxn_008 is undemonstrated and only reasonably plausible if mol_010 is defined as the aldehyde hydrate; as written it needs H2O as product. rxn_005 and rxn_012 retain the same stoichiometric problems as in P1. The literature treats imidazole-4-glycol as a side branch or sink, not an established productive intermediate en route to histidine.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_008\",\n        \"rxn_012\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Retain rxn_008 only if mol_010 is explicitly defined as the hydrate of mol_009; then write it as mol_010 -> mol_009 + H2O.\",\n        \"Split or rebalance rxn_005 with explicit H2O byproducts.\",\n        \"Use a corrected one-pot histidine step or a corrected stepwise Strecker-hydrolysis sequence.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.72,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.84,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.68,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.43,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.6,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.47,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.63,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.5,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.52,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.51,\n      \"feedback\": \"This stepwise glycol-salvage route is weaker than P2 because it adds the undemonstrated rescue of mol_010 to mol_009 before the already miswritten hydrolysis step. rxn_008 needs H2O as product if mol_010 is the hydrate; rxn_010 needs H2O as product; rxn_011 requires water as reactant and NH3 release. The route is coherent on paper, but the key salvage chemistry remains speculative in the literature.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_008\",