t terminal conversion\",\n      \"description\": \"A low-confidence rescue route in which the reported imidazole-4-glycol side branch is treated as a reservoir that can collapse back to the aldehyde before the net terminal histidine-forming step.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"name\": \"Erythrose glycol-reservoir salvage with explicit aminonitrile\",\n      \"description\": \"The same reservoir-salvage concept as P7, but with the terminal chemistry expanded into explicit Strecker capture and aminonitrile hydrolysis.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_008\", \"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"Threose glycol-reservoir salvage plus net terminal conversion\",\n      \"description\": \"Speculative threose analogue of the glycol-reservoir branch, followed by collapse to the aldehyde and the experimentally grounded net terminal conversion logic.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Threose glycol-reservoir salvage with explicit aminonitrile\",\n      \"description\": \"Most speculative route in the network: threose analogue plus glycol-reservoir rescue and explicit Strecker-hydrolysis completion.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_008\", \"mol_010\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hub_molecules\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_005\", \"mol_